From 3b788497205988b8674faac1de38192dfea8da77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:09:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 681/687] perf(dspark): reduce vocabulary-parallel greedy drafts in the
 Markov projection

The vocabulary-parallel greedy draft steps (TP > 1) materialized each
position's Markov bias shard ([requests, shard] in the head dtype) through
markov_bias_local, then reduced base + bias with greedy_markov_shard_pair.
The fused kernels that add the base logits and reduce each vocabulary tile
in the projection's epilogue (packed_vocab_markov_greedy_partials and
bf16_vocab_markov_greedy_partials, with finish_vocab_greedy_pairs) were
declared and compiled at kernel preparation but never called.

- DSparkSpeculator._sample_sequential reduces each draft position through
  DSparkDeepseekV4ForCausalLM.markov_greedy_pairs_local
  (project_head_markov_greedy_pairs into the speculator's shard pairs).
  markov_bias_local and draft_logits_local_layout, used only by the
  materialized path, are gone.
- register_warmups declares only the selections, and raises at kernel
  preparation when the Markov head does not fuse (fuses_markov_greedy: a
  TileLang packed or BF16 head, no logit scale or soft cap; an NVFP4 Markov
  head has no fused projection): no untested fallback.
- finish_vocab_greedy_pairs(top2=True) writes the runner-up that
  greedy_markov_shard_pair(top2=True) reports, to the bit: its partials keep
  one maximum per 2048-column part (GREEDY_PART), so its runner-up is the
  best maximum of the row's other parts; the fused finish reduces the tiles
  outside the pair's part. Each Markov head declares both finishes.
- Only Markov heads (tilelang_markov_head) declare the fused greedy kernels:
  prepare_bf16_head no longer compiles them for every BF16 head.

Bit-exact with the materialized path: same values, first-index ties, NaNs,
runner-ups, margins and next-step embeddings (tests below).

Tests:
- tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_vocab.py: packed and
  BF16 Markov heads at the TP4 (32320) and TP3 (43136, last rank 43008)
  shards and a partial-tile shard, BF16 and FP32 logits, top-2 on and off,
  1..64 rows, ties within and across parts, duplicate weight rows, NaNs and
  -inf rows, all four pair columns compared as bits against
  greedy_markov_shard_pair on the materialized bias; only Markov heads
  declare the kernels.
- tests/v1/worker/test_dspark_greedy_markov.py: DSparkSpeculator's
  five-position vocabulary-parallel loop through the fused projection draws
  the tokens, runner-ups, margins and Markov embeddings that the
  materialized bias and greedy_markov_shard_pair draw (TP4 and TP3 last-rank
  shards, BF16 and FP32, top-2 on and off, 1..48 requests); kernel
  preparation raises for a Markov head without the fused projection.
